     The export modes run WITHOUT a window - from make(1), from
     scripts, from a serial terminal.  vveelllluumm hands any lowercase
     -_m_o_d_e straight to the helper /usr/vellum/lib/velxport, which
     carries the model, the format and every backend and links no
     graphics at all.  On a machine with NO BITMAP CARD, run that
     helper directly: vveelllluumm itself is a graphics client and can-
     not exec where the shared graphics library is not loaded,
     even to pass its arguments on.  That is why the shipped
     Makefile skeletons say VV=/uussrr/vveelllluumm/lliibb/vveellxxppoorrtt. Each mode
     takes ONE OR MORE sheet files:

              vveelllluumm -pprriinntt f.d       Epson raster on stdout (ESC * bands,
                                      1 grid unit = 8 dots; pipe to llpprr).
                                      -wwiiddee prints landscape (the page turned a
                                      quarter), -ssccaallee _n picks n dots per
                                      grid unit - small drawings print big
              vveelllluumm -ppiicc f.d         troff pic source on stdout (16 units
                                      per inch), for figures in manuals; smooth
                                      polylines come out as pic splines
              vveelllluumm -hhppggll f.d        HPGL pen-plotter commands on stdout;
                                      the annotation layer draws in the SECOND
                                      pen (SP2) - the cheapest two-color print
                                      this machine will ever do
              vveelllluumm -ppss f.d ...      PostScript (Level 1) on stdout, one
                                      page per sheet - the laser's page.  Text
                                      is Courier sized so the monospace advance
