AASSKKIINNGG TTHHEE SSEETT
     A drawing set lives for years, and every question the shop
     asks about it - what changed, what it takes, where anything
     is, and what everything means - the set answers itself.
     These modes are the shell's, not the window's; their natural
     asker is make(1).

              vveelllluumm -ddiiffff _o_l_d _n_e_w    what CHANGED between two
                                      revisions. Matching is by IDENTITY, not by
                                      line: diff(1) on two .d files drowns in
                                      reordering, because the line order is the
                                      z-order, not the content. Symbols match by
                                      DESIGNATOR first (R7 is R7 wherever it
                                      moved in the list), everything else by
                                      exact (type, geometry, value) equality - no
                                      fuzzy matching and no tolerance: an object
                                      that moved one unit is a remove plus an
                                      add, and that is the honest answer on a
                                      grid. An object still standing exactly
                                      where it stood, saying something else,
                                      reports as CHANGED. One line each, the
                                      -check shape:
                                        new.d: R7 moved 40,20 -> 40,28
                                        new.d: R9 added (R 47k)
                                        new.d: C2 removed (C 100n)
                                        new.d: T "Supply, sheet 1" changed
                                      The EXIT STATUS is the change count (capped
                                      254), so a Makefile gates a release print
                                      on "no drift since the approved revision"
                                      exactly the way it gates on -check
              vveelllluumm -ddiiffff -mmaarrkk _o _n  ... the answer AS A DRAWING on
                                      stdout: everything unchanged on its own
                                      layers, ADDED objects bold, REMOVED objects
                                      dashed on the annotation layer. No new
                                      viewer and no new UI - the markup is
